  <data key="d13">9ce114be054738cef1ef30da393e7bb716ef16b09463247d60010b6d41701ddc</data>
  <data key="d14">ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4</data>
  <data key="d15">c7898190-020b-4332-9ebd-182c5f4dc791</data>
  <data key="d16">Eyebrows enhancing the storytelling aspect of ourillustrations.

Eyebrows complement the eyes, expanding the range of emotions conveyed and</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">boehringer-ingelheim</data>
  <data key="d5">BI Illustrations 4.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:9f23a972-9cb0-42f1-aeb5-b356adc0599b">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">55</data>
  <data key="d7">43</data>
  <data key="d8">24</data>
  <data key="d9">guidance_document</data>
  <data key="d10">0ef0e04b-9d45-4c04-bd1f-2c7827aab66e</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">BI Illustrations 4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">bd57d869c652820921c0ac1516415cef0704105f001d2b9f957b19199056a265</data>
  <data key="d14">ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4</data>
  <data key="d15">9f23a972-9cb0-42f1-aeb5-b356adc0599b</data>
  <data key="d16">of emotions through their eyes, harmonizing them with other facial features like the mouth, which fosters a sense of connection and empathybetweenthe audienceand theanimals.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">boehringer-ingelheim</data>
  <data key="d5">BI Illustrations 4.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:bbcdafd3-903c-43dd-86e4-b9e3c26398e7">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">56</data>
  <data key="d7">155</data>
  <data key="d8">24</data>
  <data key="d9">guidance_document</data>
  <data key="d10">457d8bc2-64e8-4fb7-8097-2330bb2c7a89</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">BI Illustrations 4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">c3bae6b715e977ff80f1e142afaba6893c43fe91ed3ff2db745802e3414a7327</data>
  <data key="d14">ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4</data>
  <data key="d15">bbcdafd3-903c-43dd-86e4-b9e3c26398e7</data>
  <data key="d16">The mouth, like the eyes, is fundamental for conveying emotions and feelings. We use a simplified representation of lips for both menandwomen.

Openmouth When we illustrate people talking or smiling,or we want to share a more detailed ofthemouthisblack. age,gender andethnicity. Closedmouth Don't illustrate lips more than this with facial hair-this helps to ensure there aren'ttoomanyelementsintheillustration. Mouthwithbeard When someone is fully smiling we illustrate the internal part of the mouth in white, depicting the teeth without adding too many details. Openmouth-fullteeth Mouthwithmoustache background color.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">boehringer-ingelheim</data>
  <data key="d5">BI Illustrations 4.pdf</data>
</node>
