Resource: Sunil | Name: CL-CRP-001160 | Match Text: JARDIANCE demonstrated early benefits when initiated in the hospital | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Key Message Type: Safety | Footnotes: In the EMPULSE trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 530 patients with chronic heart failure regardless of LVEF, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=265) were evaluated in the hospital setting vs placebo (n=265). The primary endpoint in the EMPULSE trial was clinical benefit, defined as a hierarchical composite of death from any cause, number of heart failure events and time to first heart failure event, or a 5-point or greater difference in change from baseline in the KCCQ-TSS at 90 days, as assessed using a win ratio. Patients treated with JARDIANCE were 36% more likely to experience clinical benefit compared with placebo (win ratio=1.36; 95% CI: 1.09, 1.68; p=0.0054).  In the EMPULSE trial, the initiation of empagliflozin for acute HF produced clinical benefit regardless of the degree of symptomatic impairment at baseline and improved</data>
