  <data key="d15">c26e4989-25b7-418a-b05e-d01c99ab8a24</data>
  <data key="d16">e BMI ≥30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate of CV death was 3.8% for JARDIANCE (n=2408) vs 4.8% for placebo (n=1213). In the BMI &lt;30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate of CV death was 3.5% for JARDIANCE (n=2279) vs 6.9% for placebo (n=1120).   RRR=relative risk reduction; ARR=absolute risk reduction; BMI=body mass index; CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; HR=hazard ratio; MACE=major adverse cardiovascular events; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes

Zinman N Engl J Med 2015 Supplement

Inzucchi Circulation 2018

