<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:06aa42bd-639c-42cd-8439-babaf800b011">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">220</data>
  <data key="d7">89</data>
  <data key="d8">65</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">8e575eb3-68c5-4fe2-9786-5cb2480351e3</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">9706153455a3c10fb9fdb6efe68591389cdbd532acb8da7d66d5ea147bf2060b</data>
  <data key="d14">b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b</data>
  <data key="d15">06aa42bd-639c-42cd-8439-babaf800b011</data>
  <data key="d16">JARDIANCE speaks to its readers/listeners much like a motivational coach who cares about his or her outcomes. JARDIANCE is not overly aggressive-it

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

is brave and energising and confident. The overall tone is optimistic and proactive, as JARDIANCE can deliver liberation to both patients and physicians-now and in the future.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:bcb3b421-23d6-41d1-9101-20b3db01d55e">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">221</data>
  <data key="d7">183</data>
  <data key="d8">65</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">c0ef518e-9d29-4fc5-bc8a-dc151bdb3e8a</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">11773d844220ddad1aa0d5b958a35ec5c987781daa6c97f810fede20869e729f</data>
  <data key="d14">b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b</data>
  <data key="d15">bcb3b421-23d6-41d1-9101-20b3db01d55e</data>
  <data key="d16">Consider the following when developing content:

-   Convey a sense of empathy with the challenges that HCPs and patients face when treating/managing the disease
-   Infuse headlines, callouts, and lead-ins with energy; use upbeat and positive language
- Speak with confidence and assuredness
-   When possible, use present and future tenses. (Note, in the EU, use past tense for all CV claims ['JARDIANCE demonstrated' vs 'JARDIANCE demonstrates']. Similarly, for safety statements in either the EU or Mexico, only past tense is acceptable.)
-   Speak directly to the reader (when appropriate), as in 'you' and 'your'
-   Start sentences or paragraphs with verbs (eg, 'Give,' 'Choose,' 'Ask') to encourage the reader to take action</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
</node>
