  <data key="d7">61</data>
  <data key="d8">31</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">60a8f800-fc0a-48cf-9014-998161e169e6</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">bbaf469df983126065d2cae71f87456d14d6e27233708f23078d6bd0bbeeede8</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d15">a9f71278-5e62-4b6a-81d6-e4fefdc7108c</data>
  <data key="d16">atinine ratio (UACR) was 175 mg/g. At baseline, approximately 81% of patients were treated with renin angiotensin system inhibitors, 65% with beta-blockers, 43% with diuretics, 77% with statins, and 86% with antiplatelet agents (mostly aspirin).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
