<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:c569da66-fa97-4972-b9c6-a9776deb6003">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">8</data>
  <data key="d7">128</data>
  <data key="d8">2</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">37fabc6d-48b2-45a0-9a39-7d25dd312d9f</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">de5bd46e76ae4125f3a003e607c977b6ade2c381be4f958b450a371d0e9b4b59</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">c569da66-fa97-4972-b9c6-a9776deb6003</data>
  <data key="d16">Jardiance is indicated in adults and children aged 10 years and above for the treatment of insufficiently controlled type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise

- -as monotherapy when metformin is considered inappropriate due to intolerance
- -in addition to other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes

For study results with respect to combination of therapies, effects on glycaemic control, cardiovascular and renal events, and the populations studied, see sections 4.4, 4.5 and 5.1.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f01f4ec7-a62a-4339-ad04-0b9e17e28cb5">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">9</data>
  <data key="d7">22</data>
  <data key="d8">2</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">916d3dd8-0293-4e83-a95d-5d42266303f7</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">4debfac06c8eaae879f6f80f3b174855a4bd8ea0f8c8ef7ce85c03b007bc7817</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">f01f4ec7-a62a-4339-ad04-0b9e17e28cb5</data>
  <data key="d16">Jardiance is indicated in adults for the treatment of symptomatic chronic heart failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:82561521-65e1-45e6-8a4f-d8de4f67acea">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">10</data>
  <data key="d7">19</data>
  <data key="d8">3</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">edf8c677-dbdf-4d72-a9f0-142c0ed443c5</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">2be97734371302bc226115c00b96dd6101acef7636980d51d14d73e99995170d</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">82561521-65e1-45e6-8a4f-d8de4f67acea</data>
  <data key="d16">Jardiance is indicated in adults for the treatment of chronic kidney disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:419da043-5237-466a-9d3a-d3a7b40c0e07">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">11</data>
  <data key="d7">102</data>
  <data key="d8">3</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">6255a9e3-f098-4b96-9800-27a1d1f3afb3</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">fbf760ccacbc4633e232ce3646e4a50d2a850bfc4b8574bf6820a1302800483a</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">419da043-5237-466a-9d3a-d3a7b40c0e07</data>
  <data key="d16">The recommended starting dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily for monotherapy and add-on combination therapy with other medicinal products for the treatment of diabetes. In patients tolerating empagliflozin 10 mg once daily who have an eGFR ≥ 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and need tighter glycaemic control, the dose can be increased to 25 mg once daily. The maximum daily dose is 25 mg (see below and section 4.4).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:24f49401-d3c7-494b-be3a-61f6c13bcac7">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">12</data>
  <data key="d7">14</data>
  <data key="d8">3</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">2dd90f41-cf84-43aa-83c1-268af0ba8aa9</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">190701bcfeae2d13c2e02833206481afa7369dcf4c958e9bd3abfc7daec30c87</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">24f49401-d3c7-494b-be3a-61f6c13bcac7</data>
  <data key="d16">The recommended dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:64c92c0a-eed1-44ae-932f-a6610959ddcc">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">13</data>
  <data key="d7">14</data>
  <data key="d8">3</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">b9f3eb9a-be8b-4f96-8f20-210ffeeee15a</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">190701bcfeae2d13c2e02833206481afa7369dcf4c958e9bd3abfc7daec30c87</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">64c92c0a-eed1-44ae-932f-a6610959ddcc</data>
  <data key="d16">The recommended dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:09805519-5f1e-4f42-b05e-23e264152436">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">14</data>
  <data key="d7">85</data>
  <data key="d8">3</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">8cc6c1c4-80dc-49ed-b160-634d92f0d22e</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">0a8a275d77d552aaca949107c5aa8217ddb189651fbb00033cbda2e4a90f7b62</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">09805519-5f1e-4f42-b05e-23e264152436</data>
  <data key="d16">When empagliflozin is used in combination with a sulphonylurea or with insulin, a lower dose of the sulphonylurea or insulin may be considered to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia (see sections 4.5 and 4.8).

If a dose is missed, it should be taken as soon as the patient remembers; however, a double dose should not be taken on the same day.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:65e6ce38-33bf-4887-8184-e1d3a60dc02c">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">15</data>
  <data key="d7">153</data>
  <data key="d8">3</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">6ff36a3a-d2f6-48b1-812d-240c5ca947ab</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1f89ccfb19ce3c851cd740502201b3549435bd585126b6fbe3b8e222e9b0517b</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">65e6ce38-33bf-4887-8184-e1d3a60dc02c</data>
  <data key="d16">Due to limited experience, it is not recommended to initiate treatment with empagliflozin in patients with an eGFR &amp;lt; 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .

In patients with an eGFR &amp;lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 the daily dose of empagliflozin is 10 mg.

In patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus, the glucose lowering efficacy of empagliflozin is reduced in patients with an eGFR &amp;lt; 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and likely absent in patients with an eGFR &amp;lt; 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . Therefore, if eGFR falls below 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2 , additional glucose lowering treatment should be considered if needed (see sections 4.4, 4.8, 5.1 and 5.2).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:55add26d-ef6a-42cd-9d55-e4214ba976af">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">16</data>
  <data key="d7">75</data>
  <data key="d8">3</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">4bec51e7-0d92-43f3-a4a8-8188f3276c3f</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">4a185f00648d92cd23c5ed1f482a8814b349ed80aa78974bb13bd23441d3fc2d</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">55add26d-ef6a-42cd-9d55-e4214ba976af</data>
  <data key="d16">No dose adjustment is required for patients with hepatic impairment. Empagliflozin exposure is increased in patients with severe hepatic impairment. Therapeutic experience in patients with severe hepatic impairment is limited and therefore not recommended for use in this population (see section 5.2).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2b8d61dc-ce25-4204-87fc-4df7cea2338b">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">17</data>
  <data key="d7">44</data>
  <data key="d8">3</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">974f594b-d029-4008-9b2c-524455fde10f</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">b8909999cc34d9188bc6a8c0c499e4f13e3f26f01ece6daee3d307243b47a286</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">2b8d61dc-ce25-4204-87fc-4df7cea2338b</data>
  <data key="d16">No dose adjustment is recommended based on age. In patients 75 years and older, an increased risk for volume depletion should be taken into account (see sections 4.4 and 4.8).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:84552a19-30f2-4233-9dff-d5b3744ce135">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">18</data>
  <data key="d7">86</data>
  <data key="d8">3</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">b0c0a9ca-1f49-4fb1-ba69-09b754e34493</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">6a9133b44fbf9738f82cca03c3d8595da9201c16f7c157c5f06cf41f62fd8175</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">84552a19-30f2-4233-9dff-d5b3744ce135</data>
  <data key="d16">The recommended starting dose is 10 mg empagliflozin once daily. In patients tolerating empagliflozin 10 mg once daily and requiring additional glycaemic control, the dose can be increased to 25 mg once daily (see sections 5.1 and 5.2). No data are available for children with eGFR &amp;lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and children below 10 years of age.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:fc704807-2fbc-44b6-abd2-3f849f9fe01f">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">19</data>
  <data key="d7">52</data>
  <data key="d8">4</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">b325c700-365c-4b74-9351-65100b30929a</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">6fc761549cecaad7b0a9e26947ab814563b33b8d1da44fc38c978373a512c96d</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">fc704807-2fbc-44b6-abd2-3f849f9fe01f</data>
  <data key="d16">The safety and efficacy of empagliflozin for the treatment of heart failure or for the treatment of chronic kidney disease in children under 18 years of age have not been established. No data are available.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:b153b93e-8521-4516-a546-2f7a966fb62c">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">20</data>
  <data key="d7">18</data>
  <data key="d8">4</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">37017a54-58ee-4218-bc2f-8d85988565e8</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">e34ae4191f33afd613c3a23272f2faf17454cd8a3fb219041202bb576834d859</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">b153b93e-8521-4516-a546-2f7a966fb62c</data>
  <data key="d16">The tablets can be taken with or without food, swallowed whole with water.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e9de16bf-ca1f-461a-8a35-5c3fee9b7fce">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">21</data>
  <data key="d7">23</data>
  <data key="d8">4</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">5655cbfa-9679-42c6-893b-4f48369d1bd5</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">8cc0fe29768569a55e0703c8413d5a145077448bca5f7426ab9084406d167fa6</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">e9de16bf-ca1f-461a-8a35-5c3fee9b7fce</data>
  <data key="d16">Hypersensitivity to the active substance or to any of the excipients listed in section 6.1.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:724bb5c2-64f5-4c48-b8a1-a102e4eff432">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">22</data>
  <data key="d7">28</data>
  <data key="d8">4</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">dff5d609-8387-412f-adb6-6b2ee91fbe2f</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">d30b144bbc5cde97bbcb20bbac30c4d28b08dd98aed4eff323f3245462894feb</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">724bb5c2-64f5-4c48-b8a1-a102e4eff432</data>
  <data key="d16">Empagliflozin should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus (see 'Ketoacidosis' in section 4.4).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:e64015b5-7cbb-47c1-a1ff-01b7c0d0102d">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">23</data>
  <data key="d7">300</data>
  <data key="d8">4</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">6b6e7cbf-c89e-484c-b82c-de150615604e</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">8058167faef7193413f8a928720e6e67f28ed521ccb306754125e92f817aab59</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">e64015b5-7cbb-47c1-a1ff-01b7c0d0102d</data>
  <data key="d16">Cases of ketoacidosis, including life-threatening and fatal cases, have been reported in patients with diabetes mellitus treated with SGLT2 inhibitors, including empagliflozin. In a number of cases, the presentation of the condition was atypical with only moderately increased blood glucose values, below 14 mmol/L (250 mg/dL). It is not known if ketoacidosis is more likely to occur with higher doses of empagliflozin. Although ketoacidosis is less likely to occur in patients without diabetes mellitus, cases have also been reported in these patients.

The risk of ketoacidosis must be considered in the event of non-specific symptoms such as nausea, vomiting, anorexia, abdominal pain, excessive thirst, difficulty breathing, confusion, unusual fatigue or sleepiness. Patients should be assessed for ketoacidosis immediately if these symptoms occur, regardless of blood glucose level.

In patients where ketoacidosis is suspected or diagnosed, treatment with empagliflozin should be discontinued immediately.

Treatment should be interrupted in patients who are hospitalised for major surgical procedures or acute serious medical illnesses. Monitoring of ketones is recommended in these patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:3db17c21-92fb-4b19-852a-0f58fded81b0">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">24</data>
  <data key="d7">300</data>
  <data key="d8">4</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">6b6e7cbf-c89e-484c-b82c-de150615604e</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">dd12a143c017125f90af3152ad89b777708ed4d7fd8217566c1d19c30470c33f</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">3db17c21-92fb-4b19-852a-0f58fded81b0</data>
  <data key="d16">tients who are hospitalised for major surgical procedures or acute serious medical illnesses. Monitoring of ketones is recommended in these patients. Measurement of blood ketone levels is preferred to urine. Treatment with empagliflozin may be restarted when the ketone values are normal and the patient's condition has stabilised.

Before initiating empagliflozin, factors in the patient history that may predispose to ketoacidosis should be considered.

Prolonged ketoacidosis and prolonged glucosuria have been observed with empagliflozin. Ketoacidosis may last longer after discontinuation of empagliflozin than expected from the plasma half-life (see section 5.2). Empagliflozin-independent factors, such as insulin deficiency, might be involved in prolonged periods of ketoacidosis.

Patients who may be at higher risk of ketoacidosis include patients with a low beta-cell function reserve (e.g. type 2 diabetes patients with low C-peptide or latent autoimmune diabetes in adults (LADA) or patients with a history of pancreatitis), patients with conditions that lead to restricted food intake or severe dehydration, patients for whom insulin doses are reduced and patients with increased insuli</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f20b0465-2f79-4044-bed9-e22153ecfe5e">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">25</data>
  <data key="d7">71</data>
  <data key="d8">4</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">6b6e7cbf-c89e-484c-b82c-de150615604e</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">7c398377f27ad1d6177c081641e06203b46a5cab18e3b5be708c258b54c8338e</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">f20b0465-2f79-4044-bed9-e22153ecfe5e</data>
  <data key="d16">h conditions that lead to restricted food intake or severe dehydration, patients for whom insulin doses are reduced and patients with increased insulin requirements due to acute medical illness, surgery or alcohol abuse. SGLT2 inhibitors should be used with caution in these patients.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ec769265-ac42-4258-a75e-a09546d34fbe">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">26</data>
  <data key="d7">124</data>
  <data key="d8">5</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">60a8b15c-9c71-4687-9f8c-b515fc74a374</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">35b07916f0a2a30a64e9b557c8d0fb1190278bfd251be693d7edd240d4cdc520</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">ec769265-ac42-4258-a75e-a09546d34fbe</data>
  <data key="d16">Restarting SGLT2 inhibitor treatment in patients with previous ketoacidosis while on SGLT2 inhibitor treatment is not recommended, unless another clear precipitating factor is identified and resolved.

Jardiance should not be used in patients with type 1 diabetes. Data from a clinical trial program in patients with type 1 diabetes showed increased ketoacidosis occurrence with common frequency in patients treated with empagliflozin 10 mg and 25 mg as an adjunct to insulin compared to placebo.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ea0884bc-6c50-4e0b-8972-b83cefb40e5b">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">27</data>
  <data key="d7">124</data>
  <data key="d8">5</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">9a7a5961-1e81-4f2f-8886-ceccb3a44061</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">eaa1b559f5ff08eb56f97c9a2b5e819c2d6e3412697e55839493b8d4b8b4b906</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">ea0884bc-6c50-4e0b-8972-b83cefb40e5b</data>
  <data key="d16">Due to limited experience, it is not recommended to initiate treatment with empagliflozin in patients with an eGFR &amp;lt; 20 mL/min/1.73 m 2 .

In patients with an eGFR &amp;lt; 60 mL/min/1.73 m 2 the daily dose of empagliflozin is 10 mg (see section 4.2).

The glucose lowering efficacy of empagliflozin is dependent on renal function, and is reduced in patients with an eGFR &amp;lt; 45 mL/min/1.73 m 2  and is likely absent in patients with an eGFR &amp;lt; 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2  (see section 4.2, 5.1 and 5.2).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:706eaa4c-937b-42c6-afa5-a13737a69019">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">28</data>
  <data key="d7">74</data>
  <data key="d8">5</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">b0a2edfb-2315-4618-b86d-09b5ed86d2c6</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">7a7e52ba2e2ca28372dfe27d45370b2eee496d760e84554280dbd3f31b63feaf</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">706eaa4c-937b-42c6-afa5-a13737a69019</data>
  <data key="d16">Assessment of renal function is recommended as follows:

- -Prior to empagliflozin initiation and periodically during treatment, i.e. at least yearly (see sections 4.2, 4.8, 5.1 and 5.2).
- -Prior to initiation of any concomitant medicinal product that may have a negative impact on renal function.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:210bca7f-6468-43cb-95cd-c413b5806ccb">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">29</data>
  <data key="d7">210</data>
  <data key="d8">5</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">4586acf2-883e-4de4-b333-63abd53adec3</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">aeff78a4c03d1fe5b97a63082478d43787ce942a54461d54ef2747b8996b7f11</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">210bca7f-6468-43cb-95cd-c413b5806ccb</data>
  <data key="d16">Based on the mode of action of SGLT2 inhibitors, osmotic diuresis accompanying glucosuria may lead to a modest decrease in blood pressure (see section 5.1). Therefore, caution should be exercised in patients for whom an empagliflozin-induced drop in blood pressure could pose a risk, such as patients with known cardiovascular disease, patients on anti-hypertensive therapy with a history of hypotension or patients aged 75 years and older.

In case of conditions that may lead to fluid loss (e.g. gastrointestinal illness), careful monitoring of volume status (e.g. physical examination, blood pressure measurements, laboratory tests including haematocrit) and electrolytes is recommended for patients receiving empagliflozin. Temporary interruption of treatment with empagliflozin should be considered until the fluid loss is corrected.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ee0a53e3-2106-4010-aa7a-ac68d63a003c">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">30</data>
  <data key="d7">138</data>
  <data key="d8">5</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">475e338e-bf52-4973-aa24-ff7b4f8be0a6</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">8d744742d9f0effdf44e410122e9a67bc5cf61adecacdac79142eed53a541eea</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">ee0a53e3-2106-4010-aa7a-ac68d63a003c</data>
  <data key="d16">The effect of empagliflozin on urinary glucose excretion is associated with osmotic diuresis, which could affect the hydration status. Patients aged 75 years and older may be at an increased risk of volume depletion. A higher number of these patients treated with empagliflozin had adverse reactions related to volume depletion as compared to placebo (see section 4.8). Therefore, special attention should be given to their volume intake in case of co-administered medicinal products which may lead to volume depletion (e.g. diuretics, ACE inhibitors).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1117bd18-288c-4f1e-9dbb-10cb65211614">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">31</data>
  <data key="d7">69</data>
  <data key="d8">5</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">7e20fc68-1213-476f-b61f-bdcd7057e1d2</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">2ae2c4834c169d6f1021344721d14a2d21708cf186186b57df174985df38e59a</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">1117bd18-288c-4f1e-9dbb-10cb65211614</data>
  <data key="d16">Cases of complicated urinary tract infections including pyelonephritis and urosepsis have been reported in patients treated with empagliflozin (see section 4.8). Temporary interruption of empagliflozin should be considered in patients with complicated urinary tract infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a239be01-78cb-4ee1-a69e-00bf85412e9d">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">32</data>
  <data key="d7">194</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">d7aa5df9-51be-4cc9-8074-350839411d7e</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">5985f7747dfc1f3cfc863c4596f01057910579577b195523326a1db2cc33c53b</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">a239be01-78cb-4ee1-a69e-00bf85412e9d</data>
  <data key="d16">Cases of necrotising fasciitis of the perineum, (also known as Fournier's gangrene), have been reported in female and male patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors, including empagliflozin. This is a rare but serious and potentially life-threatening event that requires urgent surgical intervention and antibiotic treatment.

Patients should be advised to seek medical attention if they experience a combination of symptoms of pain, tenderness, erythema, or swelling in the genital or perineal area, with fever or malaise. Be aware that either uro-genital infection or perineal abscess may precede necrotising fasciitis. If Fournier´s gangrene is suspected, Jardiance should be discontinued and prompt treatment (including antibiotics and surgical debridement) should be instituted.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a5383fb1-0777-4de0-80e7-d55488aa06b1">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">33</data>
  <data key="d7">76</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">5556d121-5d2f-42f5-b6cb-3847d4b3223a</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">93d0fe0887a904b38d0cbf27860b0d322b3dcf519bfd68bb589d2bca5a771a9b</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">a5383fb1-0777-4de0-80e7-d55488aa06b1</data>
  <data key="d16">An increase in cases of lower limb amputation (primarily of the toe) has been observed in long-term clinical studies with another SGLT2 inhibitor. It is unknown whether this constitutes a class effect. Like for all diabetic patients it is important to counsel patients on routine preventative foot-care.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2fa17cee-f4b2-474c-a65d-aaad1e9562d0">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">34</data>
  <data key="d7">42</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">8e7aa7a7-a2fc-4f07-bc81-4bc7d82f836f</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">97444a01835032b053bbbf0457abdde49027ed4fce29b14b0d540c50b5c89191</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">2fa17cee-f4b2-474c-a65d-aaad1e9562d0</data>
  <data key="d16">Cases of hepatic injury have been reported with empagliflozin in clinical trials. A causal relationship between empagliflozin and hepatic injury has not been established.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:88d74940-6f28-41a1-bd62-6d4265d2fc7d">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">35</data>
  <data key="d7">52</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">8d5b8aa6-3e6a-4322-9090-a3afe8d4122a</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">587ae7ba9f721c14ae0424660af0252e8ba2a03bde2018134e2817e0d768f311</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">88d74940-6f28-41a1-bd62-6d4265d2fc7d</data>
  <data key="d16">Haematocrit increase was observed with empagliflozin treatment (see section 4.8). Patients with pronounced elevations in haematocrit should be monitored and investigated for underlying haematological disease.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5d383eef-d990-47ea-ad53-a18d9aabda16">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">36</data>
  <data key="d7">19</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">9fbfe13b-d7e9-47c8-b364-22200e5553b5</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">5bea05e549b4802b2f157c0eee8181330e4c82a241947d655eb2dc779734fcf4</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">5d383eef-d990-47ea-ad53-a18d9aabda16</data>
  <data key="d16">Patients with albuminuria may benefit more from treatment with empagliflozin.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:79fd6a68-a8fa-4005-ad59-e4b82e14bbca">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">37</data>
  <data key="d7">42</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">e4c9d7e4-676c-4ba6-bd7a-a90f0344acc1</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">0a9ac263672c4798577daf2aa9b1c0dbf0a01cbf7354b74a39bb7f4e4387701a</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">79fd6a68-a8fa-4005-ad59-e4b82e14bbca</data>
  <data key="d16">Patients with infiltrative disease or with Takotsubo cardiomyopathy have not been specifically studied. Therefore, efficacy in these patients has not been established.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a1120350-3bb9-4b2a-bc9a-15e0c800b349">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">38</data>
  <data key="d7">26</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">0b339ebd-6013-461d-a133-bd7675c8493b</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">446a5a1ddaf1d9d53f53941ae73b53cd2a705a441ed5aee262b461c761a43db8</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">a1120350-3bb9-4b2a-bc9a-15e0c800b349</data>
  <data key="d16">Due to its mechanism of action, patients taking Jardiance will test positive for glucose in their urine.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:cbc00ef9-b6da-4e9a-b83e-8b6201817834">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">39</data>
  <data key="d7">60</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">77d73b63-98f8-4f3b-b9ad-840ab3692dc6</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">42a63c16f3f7d42df5e6e164b7fc3de25444cb7b8f269c9e2300ff2675c5e5d9</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">cbc00ef9-b6da-4e9a-b83e-8b6201817834</data>
  <data key="d16">Monitoring glycaemic control with 1,5-AG assay is not recommended as measurements of 1,5-AG are unreliable in assessing glycaemic control in patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors. Use of alternative methods to monitor glycaemic control is advised.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:f361aba0-8837-4c34-8557-f711b93faeb6">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">40</data>
  <data key="d7">48</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">74ddfc00-f218-4899-bfc5-81fa0c1e64da</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">950d9a0393385b8fd53b5ca9cbbf7ea3b3e90e9b0a051629f5557e0068bb6763</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">f361aba0-8837-4c34-8557-f711b93faeb6</data>
  <data key="d16">The tablets contain lactose. Patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medicinal product.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:07bf460e-91f0-453a-b247-b84cd724b500">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">41</data>
  <data key="d7">24</data>
  <data key="d8">6</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">d26fc014-0c55-4945-b1cc-c866c2258dc3</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">f3356ddad3fc2c51e23667c158b91b3b95adf0b11ca4b950582c955bf1b3d74e</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">07bf460e-91f0-453a-b247-b84cd724b500</data>
  <data key="d16">Each tablet contains less than 1 mmol sodium (23 mg), that is to say essentially 'sodium free'.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:106da502-2fb9-4c91-8a1b-7bfbe5bef5ea">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">42</data>
  <data key="d7">38</data>
  <data key="d8">7</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">b9908a1a-c9e1-4cfc-ad05-9bd4f2b282f3</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">d3e1b93d040e0e53143aba6c6bb58c4d882a8986540c7337b25952dd15431ec5</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">106da502-2fb9-4c91-8a1b-7bfbe5bef5ea</data>
  <data key="d16">Empagliflozin may add to the diuretic effect of thiazide and loop diuretics and may increase the risk of dehydration and hypotension (see section 4.4).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:acbf3404-2548-4e71-806a-1b73f6a7cef3">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">43</data>
  <data key="d7">71</data>
  <data key="d8">7</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">e0799d46-0074-47d9-b4db-2580f1a1d3ff</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">d861f906d7b7758c45fa8d639bfa404cb184490ce5926088810127d14b76250e</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">acbf3404-2548-4e71-806a-1b73f6a7cef3</data>
  <data key="d16">Insulin and insulin secretagogues, such as sulphonylureas, may increase the risk of hypoglycaemia. Therefore, a lower dose of insulin or an insulin secretagogue may be required to reduce the risk of hypoglycaemia when used in combination with empagliflozin (see sections 4.2 and 4.8).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:ff427777-0463-4683-9c7e-2a1b0b8fb47c">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">44</data>
  <data key="d7">300</data>
  <data key="d8">7</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">f92f4b0d-f96a-4cd5-9830-ecd27c66c021</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">602a3b094ca31d1abdf4e4ca91b2bf34382ffa8cc3b1a60b75f24b49d66d5e42</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">ff427777-0463-4683-9c7e-2a1b0b8fb47c</data>
  <data key="d16">In vitro data suggest that the primary route of metabolism of empagliflozin in humans is glucuronidation by uridine 5'-diphosphoglucuronosyltransferases UGT1A3, UGT1A8, UGT1A9, and UGT2B7. Empagliflozin is a substrate of the human uptake transporters OAT3, OATP1B1, and OATP1B3, but not OAT1 and OCT2. Empagliflozin is a substrate of P-glycoprotein (P-gp) and breast cancer resistance protein (BCRP).

Co-administration of empagliflozin with probenecid, an inhibitor of UGT enzymes and OAT3, resulted in a 26% increase in peak empagliflozin plasma concentrations (Cmax) and a 53% increase in area under the concentration-time curve (AUC). These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.

The effect of UGT induction (e.g. induction by rifampicin or phenytoin) on empagliflozin has not been studied. Co-treatment with known inducers of UGT enzymes is not recommended due to a potential risk of decreased efficacy. If an inducer of these UGT enzymes must be co-administered, monitoring of glycaemic control to assess response to Jardiance is appropriate.

An interaction study with gemfibrozil, an in vitro inhibitor of OAT3 and OATP1B1/1B3 transporters, showed that empagliflozin Cmax i</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:4ad325b7-71ff-4416-9ab7-e42f23add2da">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">45</data>
  <data key="d7">241</data>
  <data key="d8">7</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">f92f4b0d-f96a-4cd5-9830-ecd27c66c021</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">0af41f9d532b76c2ddf545e3ccf70fe587a4f168d948de037c39d47ef40022f4</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">4ad325b7-71ff-4416-9ab7-e42f23add2da</data>
  <data key="d16">e is appropriate.

An interaction study with gemfibrozil, an in vitro inhibitor of OAT3 and OATP1B1/1B3 transporters, showed that empagliflozin Cmax increased by 15% and AUC increased by 59% following coadministration. These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.

Inhibition of OATP1B1/1B3 transporters by co-administration with rifampicin resulted in a 75% increase in Cmax and a 35% increase in AUC of empagliflozin. These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.

Empagliflozin exposure was similar with and without co-administration with verapamil, a P-gp inhibitor, indicating that inhibition of P-gp does not have any clinically relevant effect on empagliflozin.

Interaction studies suggest that the pharmacokinetics of empagliflozin were not influenced by coadministration with metformin, glimepiride, pioglitazone, sitagliptin, linagliptin, warfarin, verapamil, ramipril, simvastatin, torasemide and hydrochlorothiazide.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:8ef5f428-bb1a-4376-bdfd-a2ce8519f6d0">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">46</data>
  <data key="d7">169</data>
  <data key="d8">7</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">4108c328-e013-4b32-8dd6-9c87d990eeb6</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">240391e5bf1e684e12be2670970df2314be3f78b5ffc4c2f7320b411ee92a53b</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">8ef5f428-bb1a-4376-bdfd-a2ce8519f6d0</data>
  <data key="d16">Empagliflozin may increase renal lithium excretion and the blood lithium levels may be decreased. Serum concentration of lithium should be monitored more frequently after empagliflozin initiation and dose changes. Please refer the patient to the lithium prescribing doctor in order to monitor serum concentration of lithium.

Based on in vitro studies, empagliflozin does not inhibit, inactivate, or induce CYP450 isoforms. Empagliflozin does not inhibit UGT1A1, UGT1A3, UGT1A8, UGT1A9, or UGT2B7. Drug-drug interactions involving the major CYP450 and UGT isoforms with empagliflozin and concomitantly administered substrates of these enzymes are therefore considered unlikely.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:21f22924-ce3e-4ec1-85c5-d7b32485150b">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">47</data>
  <data key="d7">232</data>
  <data key="d8">8</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">df6f1ec4-ed31-428c-96e4-b3942a882073</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">fc434ea7f23c3466a6cd104b96594a7d5a36f3bbac688a4f87e6c7589427c830</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">21f22924-ce3e-4ec1-85c5-d7b32485150b</data>
  <data key="d16">Empagliflozin does not inhibit P-gp at therapeutic doses. Based on in vitro studies, empagliflozin is considered unlikely to cause interactions with active substances that are P-gp substrates. Coadministration of digoxin, a P-gp substrate, with empagliflozin resulted in a 6% increase in AUC and 14% increase in Cmax of digoxin. These changes were not considered to be clinically meaningful.

Empagliflozin does not inhibit human uptake transporters such as OAT3, OATP1B1, and OATP1B3 in vitro at clinically relevant plasma concentrations and, as such, drug-drug interactions with substrates of these uptake transporters are considered unlikely.

Interaction studies conducted in healthy volunteers suggest that empagliflozin had no clinically relevant effect on the pharmacokinetics of metformin, glimepiride, pioglitazone, sitagliptin, linagliptin, simvastatin, warfarin, ramipril, digoxin, diuretics and oral contraceptives.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:a0a256d6-17cc-471d-aa8e-0d063637a465">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">48</data>
  <data key="d7">14</data>
  <data key="d8">8</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">cb2b9b2f-45b4-4e99-845e-431bd31dce18</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">27d91298937e9be3835721f0bf7f967649f1c06c5a485887df615f044da18d70</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">a0a256d6-17cc-471d-aa8e-0d063637a465</data>
  <data key="d16">Interaction studies have only been performed in adults.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:678dd59e-4249-438e-b9f5-4e8c42ea6ecc">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">49</data>
  <data key="d7">115</data>
  <data key="d8">8</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">689d954c-5fa0-4db4-a085-143676834c2e</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">2243b070af48330f5e986ab82e1002b4b36f105cdc37a13160c3c03a88dff0dc</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">678dd59e-4249-438e-b9f5-4e8c42ea6ecc</data>
  <data key="d16">There are no data from the use of empagliflozin in pregnant women. Animal studies show that empagliflozin crosses the placenta during late gestation to a very limited extent but do not indicate direct or indirect harmful effects with respect to early embryonic development. However, animal studies have shown adverse effects on postnatal development (see section 5.3). As a precautionary measure, it is preferable to avoid the use of Jardiance during pregnancy.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:0d446b35-c4ef-4b47-89c0-9364003dec2b">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">50</data>
  <data key="d7">66</data>
  <data key="d8">8</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">c37b5864-2d1a-4473-9a4b-60505cdcb9de</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">7ffdc510b843b7a4b5a87568b94577b5578f6697eff134000a7752980d39f634</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">0d446b35-c4ef-4b47-89c0-9364003dec2b</data>
  <data key="d16">No data in humans are available on excretion of empagliflozin into milk. Available toxicological data in animals have shown excretion of empagliflozin in milk. A risk to the newborns/infants cannot be excluded. Jardiance should not be used during breast-feeding.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:2e4beaf8-c05f-4119-bed1-853e7ecf4274">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">51</data>
  <data key="d7">47</data>
  <data key="d8">8</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">962bc2f9-25df-4d79-9e71-ac8e9c5c24e1</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">ddfdbd7026027e78e0d26ca860ccafade9798208d82eef7d3bf61a1e0d46d05b</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">2e4beaf8-c05f-4119-bed1-853e7ecf4274</data>
  <data key="d16">No studies on the effect on human fertility have been conducted for Jardiance. Animal studies do not indicate direct or indirect harmful effects with respect to fertility (see section 5.3).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:9b2f2330-1b44-4683-8d29-4e6382386cb9">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">52</data>
  <data key="d7">66</data>
  <data key="d8">8</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">b9b6bedd-2c81-45d4-aec9-4e0963368e04</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">f927d5c4b40a4900f2b64c5668fe015439ae9ba084b9db5e7f92c9a506442cc6</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">9b2f2330-1b44-4683-8d29-4e6382386cb9</data>
  <data key="d16">Jardiance has minor influence on the ability to drive and use machines. Patients should be advised to take precautions to avoid hypoglycaemia while driving and using machines, in particular when Jardiance is used in combination with a sulphonylurea and/or insulin.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:7661a4a7-33eb-49b0-9db8-0a22712b3866">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">53</data>
  <data key="d7">96</data>
  <data key="d8">8</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">bc93c8a3-3eb1-4c6d-bf5b-9db9c5014c62</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">11444b2903aade028e7f9ac62052c4fb35dfaeb03914c9e39a9b8c858c164f2c</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">7661a4a7-33eb-49b0-9db8-0a22712b3866</data>
  <data key="d16">A total of 15 582 patients with type 2 diabetes were included in clinical studies to evaluate the safety of empagliflozin, of which 10 004 patients received empagliflozin, either alone or in combination with metformin, a sulphonylurea, pioglitazone, DPP-4 inhibitors, or insulin.

In 6 placebo-controlled trials of 18 to 24 weeks duration, 3 534 patients were included of which 1 183</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:684fd73b-9067-4046-87a2-b56d5157409a">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">54</data>
  <data key="d7">78</data>
  <data key="d8">9</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">d298fc33-3414-4a64-bbf1-6c158b856f90</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">9ec8914792f2a0494ec5d45bd124aa5cea8cb44b87f9daf202ddcf6dc74065c6</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">684fd73b-9067-4046-87a2-b56d5157409a</data>
  <data key="d16">were treated with placebo and 2 351 with empagliflozin. The overall incidence of adverse events in patients treated with empagliflozin was similar to placebo. The most frequently reported adverse reaction was hypoglycaemia when used with sulphonylurea or insulin (see description of selected adverse reactions).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:07bc97f0-8b8a-4cfb-9cc7-b22d0b881d9b">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">55</data>
  <data key="d7">105</data>
  <data key="d8">9</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">e9e280b4-7d10-4662-aa4f-cd53e6d91934</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">aa1792435f615426a5a598b7eea141f6d7c3c9805c0d68026b2ea9fb9e290c49</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">07bc97f0-8b8a-4cfb-9cc7-b22d0b881d9b</data>
  <data key="d16">The EMPEROR studies included patients with heart failure and either reduced ejection fraction (N = 3 726) or preserved ejection fraction (N = 5 985) treated with empagliflozin 10 mg or placebo. Approximately half of the patients had type 2 diabetes mellitus. The most frequent adverse reaction of the pooled EMPEROR-Reduced and EMPEROR-Preserved studies was volume depletion (empagliflozin 10 mg: 11.4%. placebo: 9.7%).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:5e876b5d-994a-4ee4-a7bc-7aa6c2a3a1e5">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">56</data>
  <data key="d7">127</data>
  <data key="d8">9</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">cb94014e-4890-475c-a97d-12b74bc2cc8b</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">618fb652b45b6dfef667310189f508518edb9529e63ffad0ad50729e9823182a</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">5e876b5d-994a-4ee4-a7bc-7aa6c2a3a1e5</data>
  <data key="d16">The EMPA-KIDNEY study included patients with chronic kidney disease (N = 6 609) treated with 10 mg empagliflozin or placebo. About 44% of the patients had type 2 diabetes mellitus. The most frequent adverse events in the EMPA-KIDNEY study were gout (empagliflozin 7.0% vs placebo 8.0%), and acute kidney injury (empagliflozin 2.8% vs placebo 3.5%) which were more frequently reported in patients on placebo.

The overall safety profile of empagliflozin was generally consistent across the studied indications.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:chunk:1b2b0da2-e1dc-436a-877d-a80a85c8e548">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">57</data>
  <data key="d7">300</data>
  <data key="d8">9</data>
