  <data key="d13">59b7e180fb7067cbb0a08a76ceafc9aa73fb55ddd11ff72ca667d7bbcacac670</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d15">99b19e85-0e1c-47c0-8ebd-2c4bb47a3332</data>
  <data key="d16">: 37.2% during initial 18 weeks treatment when insulin could not be adjusted; empagliflozin 10 mg: 51.1%, empagliflozin 25 mg: 57.7%, placebo: 58% over the 52-week trial).

In the EMPEROR heart failure studies, similar frequency of hypoglycaemia was noted when used addon to sulphonylurea or insulin (empagliflozin 10 mg: 6.5%, placebo: 6.7%).</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
