  <data key="d25">candidate</data>
  <data key="d26">Guideline / Standard of care</data>
  <data key="d27">Key inclusion criteria included a chronic HF (NYHA class II-IV) diagnosis, an elevated NT-proBNP level, and structural heart changes or documented hospitalisation for HF within 12 months. Elevated NT-proBNP is defined as a level of &gt;300 pg/mL or, for patients with atrial fibrillation at baseline, a level of &gt;900 pg/mL.2</data>
  <data key="d28">5812fcb9-1028-4304-99d1-d1da70d2fc48</data>
