  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d33">HCP/Internal</data>
  <data key="d24">candidate</data>
  <data key="d25">candidate</data>
  <data key="d26">Mechanism of action</data>
  <data key="d27">Used alone” is defined as giving JARDIANCE without insulin or sulphonylureas.2 

|| The mechanism of action of JARDIANCE is dependent on blood glucose levels, meaning it only removes glucose when levels are elevated. The risk of hypoglycaemia only increases when it’s combined with other medications that can cause low blood sugar, such as insulin or sulphonylureas.2,3</data>
  <data key="d28">5812fcb9-1028-4304-99d1-d1da70d2fc48</data>
  <data key="d9">claims_content_modules</data>
