<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:02c3962f-9738-4add-a977-b0e43fdc0272">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">HIGHLIGHTS OF PRESCRIBING INFORMATION</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">02c3962f-9738-4add-a977-b0e43fdc0272</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">These highlights do not include all the information needed to use JARDIANCE safely and effectively. See full prescribing information for JARDIANCE.

JARDIANCE ®  (empagliflozin tablets), for oral use

Initial U.S. Approval: 2014</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:7ef8c3e1-ee2d-467d-84af-eeda2efb8f1a">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">---------------------------RECENT MAJOR CHANGES---------------------------</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">7ef8c3e1-ee2d-467d-84af-eeda2efb8f1a</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">Warnings and Precautions (5.3)

10/2025</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:a0d22c6f-3704-402a-8bef-b0039f4472c1">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">----------------------------INDICATIONS AND USAGE---------------------------</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">a0d22c6f-3704-402a-8bef-b0039f4472c1</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">JARDIANCE is a sodium-glucose co-transporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitor indicated:

- x To reduce the risk of cardiovascular death and hospitalization for heart failure in adults with heart failure. (1)
- x To reduce the risk of sustained decline in eGFR, end-stage kidney disease, cardiovascular death, and hospitalization in adults with chronic kidney disease at risk of progression. (1)
- x To reduce the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus and established cardiovascular disease. (1)
- x As an adjunct to diet and exercise to improve glycemic control in adults and pediatric patients aged 10 years and older with type 2 diabetes mellitus. (1)</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:ad7eaca9-7cd2-4fa9-b9c1-052b1adb8aad">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Limitations of Use:</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">ad7eaca9-7cd2-4fa9-b9c1-052b1adb8aad</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">- x Not recommended for use to improve glycemic control in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus. It may increase the risk of diabetic ketoacidosis in these patients. (1)
- x Not recommended for use to improve glycemic control in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus with an eGFR less than 30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 . (1)
- x Not recommended for the treatment of chronic kidney disease in patients with polycystic kidney disease or patients requiring or with a recent history of intravenous immunosuppressive therapy or greater than 45 mg of prednisone or equivalent for kidney disease. JARDIANCE is not expected to be effective in these populations. (1)</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:862c2857-c3db-4b79-917f-521b8ba93688">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">----------------------DOSAGE AND ADMINISTRATION-----------------------</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">862c2857-c3db-4b79-917f-521b8ba93688</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">- x Assess renal function before initiating and as clinically indicated. Assess volume status and correct volume depletion before initiating. (2.1)
- x Recommended dosage is 10 mg orally once daily in the morning, taken with or without food. (2.2)
- x For additional glycemic control, dosage may be increased to 25 mg orally once daily in patients tolerating JARDIANCE. (2.2)
- x Withhold JARDIANCE for at least 3 days, if possible, prior to surgery or procedures associated with prolonged fasting. (2.3)
- x Hypersensitivity to empagliflozin or any of the excipients in JARDIANCE. (4)</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:f2361244-a5ac-459c-a1aa-f6622f08fb34">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">---------------------DOSAGE FORMS AND STRENGTHS----------------------</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">f2361244-a5ac-459c-a1aa-f6622f08fb34</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">Tablets: 10 mg, 25 mg (3)</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:61886f3e-6fdd-4d86-bf7f-c0cf3291cbec">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">-------------------------------CONTRAINDICATIONS------------------------------</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">61886f3e-6fdd-4d86-bf7f-c0cf3291cbec</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16"></data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:034c5600-3a9e-4f0e-86d6-8db16ed2a246">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">-----------------------WARNINGS AND PRECAUTIONS------------------------</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">034c5600-3a9e-4f0e-86d6-8db16ed2a246</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">- x Diabetic Ketoacidosis in Patients with Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus and Other Ketoacidosis: Consider ketone monitoring in patients with type 1 diabetes mellitus and consider ketone monitoring in others at risk for ketoacidosis, as indicated. Assess for ketoacidosis regardless of presenting blood glucose levels and discontinue JARDIANCE if ketoacidosis is suspected. Monitor patients for resolution of ketoacidosis before restarting. (5.1)
- x Volume Depletion: Before initiating JARDIANCE, assess volume status and renal function in patients with impaired renal function, elderly patients, or patients on loop diuretics. Monitor for signs and symptoms during therapy. (5.2)
- x Genitourinary Infections, including Urosepsis, Pyelonephritis, Necrotizing Fasciitis of the Perineum (Fournier's Gangrene), and Genital Mycotic Infections: Monitor patients for signs and symptoms of genitourinary infections and treat promptly, if indicated. Immediately evaluate patients presenting with pain or tenderness, erythema, or swelling in the genital or perineal area, along with fever or malaise, for necrotizing fasciitis and if suspected, discontinue JARDIANCE, and promptly institute appropriate medical and/or surgical intervention. (5.3)
- x Hypoglycemia: Adult patients taking an insulin secretagogue or insulin may have an increased risk of hypoglycemia. In pediatric patients 10 years of age and older, the risk of hypoglycemia was higher regardless of insulin use. Consider lowering the dosage of insulin secretagogue or insulin to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia when initiating JARDIANCE. (5.4)
- x Lower Limb Amputation: Monitor patients for infections or ulcers of lower limbs, and institute appropriate treatment (5.5)
- x Hypersensitivity Reactions: Serious hypersensitivity reactions (e.g., angioedema) have occurred with JARDIANCE. If hypersensitivity reactions occur, discontinue JARDIANCE, treat promptly, and monitor until signs and symptoms resolve. (5.6)</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:8464457d-e8da-4e8c-8d69-4e56ccc126e7">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">------------------------------ADVERSE REACTIONS-------------------------------</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">8464457d-e8da-4e8c-8d69-4e56ccc126e7</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">Most common adverse reactions (5% or greater incidence) were urinary tract infections and female genital mycotic infections (6.1)

To report SUSPECTED ADVERSE REACTIONS, contact Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc. at 1-800-542-6257 or FDA at 1-800-FDA1088 or www.fda.gov/medwatch .</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:1dc1786d-68b0-486f-a2a6-f4a38d5d6614">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">------------------------------DRUG INTERACTIONS-------------------------------</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">1dc1786d-68b0-486f-a2a6-f4a38d5d6614</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">See full prescribing information for information on drug interactions and interference of JARDIANCE with laboratory tests. (7)</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:pisection:19829346-10c0-4e65-a3e2-d5e9a3651c59">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">-----------------------USE IN SPECIFIC POPULATIONS------------------------</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">19829346-10c0-4e65-a3e2-d5e9a3651c59</data>
  <data key="d12">Jardiance_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b2560bb2-851a-4e06-8246-07641712e8b0</data>
  <data key="d16">- x Pregnancy: Advise females of the potential risk to a fetus especially during the second and third trimesters. (8.1)
- x Lactation: Not recommended when breastfeeding. (8.2)
- x Geriatric Patients: Higher incidence of adverse reactions related to volume depletion and reduced renal function. (8.5)
- x Renal Impairment: Higher incidence of adverse reactions related to reduced renal function. (8.6)

See 17 for PATIENT COUNSELING INFORMATION and Medication Guide.

Revised: 10/2025

