Resource: Moumita | Name: CL-CRP-001484 | Match Text: In patients with T2D and eCVD, JARDIANCE reduced risk of CV death regardless of patients’ HbA1c or BMI. | Country of Origin: Corporate | Brand: JARDIANCE | Therapeutic Area: Metabolism | Lifecycle State: Approved for Use | Indication: Type 2 diabetes mellitus | Key Message Type: Efficacy | End Audience: HCP (Health Care Personnel) | Footnotes: In the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 7720 patients with T2D at high cardiovascular risk, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg (n=4867) were evaluated vs placebo (n=2333). Patients were adults with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke. The primary composite outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial was 3-point MACE, composed of death from CV causes, nonfatal MI, or nonfatal stroke, as analysed in the pooled JARDIANCE group vs the placebo group. The 14% RRR (1.6% ARR) in 3-point MACE (HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99; p&lt;0.001 for noninferiority; p=0.04 for superiority) was driven by a reduction in the risk of CV death (HR=0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77); there was no change in risk of nonfatal MI (HR=0.87; 95% CI: 0.70, 1.09) or nonfatal stroke (HR=1.24; 95% CI: 0.92, 1.67).  A prespecified analysis included subgroups of patients with HbA1c &lt;8.5% and ≥8.5%  Rate of CV death (%) across HbA1c subgroups: All values depict JARDIANCE vs placebo, respectively. &lt;7.0%: 2.4 (n=297) vs 7.9 (n=127); 7.0%-&lt;8.0%: 3.7 (n=2042) vs 6.1 (n=1029); 8.0%-&lt;9.0%: 3.7 (n=1534) vs 5.4 (n=795); ≥9.0%: 4.2 (n=812) vs 5.5 (n=382).  Rate of CV death across BMI subgroups: In the BMI ≥30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate of CV death was 3.8% for JARDIANCE (n=2408) vs 4.8% for placebo (n=1213). In the BMI &lt;30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate of CV death was 3.5% for JARDIANCE (n=2279) vs 6.9% for placebo (n=1120).   RRR=relative risk reduction; ARR=absolute risk reduction; BMI=body mass index; CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; HR=hazard ratio; MACE=major adverse cardiovascular events; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; T2D=type 2 diabetes | Reference: 2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes

Zinman N Engl J Med 2015 Supplement

Inzucchi Circulation 2018

