#: 120 | Final Corrected Claim: *Key inclusion criteria included a chronic HF (NYHA class II-IV) diagnosis, an elevated NT-proBNP level, and therapy with the appropriate doses of HF medication. Elevated NT-proBNP is defined as a level of ≥1000 pg/mL in those with an ejection fraction of 31% to 35% or a level of ≥2500 pg/mL in those with an ejection fraction of 36% to 40%, as compared with a level of ≥600 pg/mL in those with an ejection fraction of ≤30%. | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology, Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 Card iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.85; 2026 Card iVA p.157; 2026 PCP iVA p.105 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: See source asset footnotes and local label. | Reference: 2026 Card iVA; 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.85; 2026 Card iVA p.157; 2026 PCP iVA p.105
#: 121 | Final Corrected Claim: In a subgroup analysis at 24 weeks of patients with baseline BMI ≥35, adjusted mean changes in weight were -0.34 kg for placebo (n=29), -2.63 kg for JARDIANCE 10 mg (n=33), and -3.35 kg for JARDIANCE 25 mg (n=41). Difference from placebo (adjusted mean) was -2.28 for JARDIANCE 10 mg and -3.01 for JARDIANCE 25 mg. | Status: Corrected | Indication: General | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Quantitative detail: 25 mg; 10 mg | Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 3 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA; 2026 Endo iVA p.57; 2026 PCP iVA p.36
