#: 183 | Final Corrected Claim: Treat early to reduce the risk of hospitalisation or CV death in your patients3 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Campaign / Messaging | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.5; 2026 Card iVA p.50 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 3 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.5; 2026 Card iVA p.50
#: 184 | Final Corrected Claim: reduce their risk of hospitalisation or CV death5,6 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Campaign / Messaging | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 PCP iVA p.57 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 5,6 | Reference: 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 PCP iVA p.57
#: 185 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE can help you stay committed by: offering protection by reducing the risk of CV death for adult patients with T2D + eCVD; reducing the risk of CV death and HHF for adult patients with HF; reducing the risk of kidney disease progression or CV death in adult patients with CKD; and lowering HbA1c in adult patients with T2D.1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Campaign / Messaging | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Endocrinology, Primary Care | Source asset(s): 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | Page(s): 2026 Endo iVA p.1; 2026 PCP iVA p.1 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Endo iVA; 2026 PCP iVA | 2026 Endo iVA p.1; 2026 PCP iVA p.1
#: 186 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE can help you stay committed by: offering protection by reducing the risk of CV death for adult patients with eCVD + T2D; reducing the risk of CV death and HHF for adult patients with HF; reducing the risk of kidney disease progression or CV death in adult patients with CKD; and lowering HbA1c in adult patients with T2D.1 | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Campaign / Messaging | End Audience: HCP/Internal | Contextual Information: Specialty context: Cardiology | Source asset(s): 2026 Card iVA | Page(s): 2026 Card iVA p.1 | Extracted only from the included 2026 iVAs; local medical, legal and regulatory validation is required. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: 2026 Card iVA | 2026 Card iVA p.1
#: 187 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE can help you stay committed by: offering protection by reducing the risk of CV death for adult patients with T2D + eCVD; reducing the risk of CV death and HHF for adult patients with HF; reducing the risk of kidney disease progression or CV death in adult patients with CKD; and lowering HbA1c in adult patients with T2D. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: 2026 Nephrology iVA overarching benefit statement. Local label and mandatory qualifiers must be checked before reuse. Source: PC-CRP-105591, page 1. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: JARDIANCE Summary of Product Characteristics, June 2025 | PC-CRP-105591 Nephrology iVA 2026, p.1
#: 188 | Final Corrected Claim: Your patients with CKD are more likely to die from CVD than to progress to kidney failure. Nearly 1 in 2 patients with CKD will die from CVD before reaching end-stage kidney disease and requiring dialysis. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Disease-burden statement; not a product efficacy claim. Source: PC-CRP-105591 Nephrology iVA 2026, page 5. | Footnotes: 1,2 | Reference: PC-CRP-105591 Nephrology iVA 2026, p.5
#: 189 | Final Corrected Claim: CV mortality risk is elevated even at low albuminuria levels. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Disease education / Unmet need | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: CKD disease-risk statement based on albuminuria and kidney function risk stratification. Source: PC-CRP-105591, page 8. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: PC-CRP-105591 Nephrology iVA 2026, p.8
#: 190 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE provides kidney and CV protection as demonstrated in multiple clinical trials spanning a decade. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Heart failure; Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Umbrella statement linked to EMPA-REG OUTCOME, EMPEROR-Reduced, EMPEROR-Preserved and EMPA-KIDNEY. Must be used with indication-specific outcomes and footnotes. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 14–17. | Footnotes: 1-5 | Reference: EMPA-REG OUTCOME | EMPEROR-Reduced | EMPEROR-Preserved | EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.14-17
#: 191 | Final Corrected Claim: In EMPA-KIDNEY, JARDIANCE reduced the risk of kidney disease progression or cardiovascular death by 28% versus placebo. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: EMPA-KIDNEY primary composite endpoint: HR=0.72; 95% CI: 0.64, 0.82; p&lt;0.001. Use with complete trial population and standard-of-care qualifiers. Source: PC-CRP-105591, page 18. | Footnotes: 1,3 | Reference: Herrington WG et al. N Engl J Med. 2023; 388:117-127 | EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.18-20
#: 192 | Final Corrected Claim: EMPA-KIDNEY studied JARDIANCE across a broad spectrum of patients with CKD, including understudied patient populations. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Clinical evidence / Study population | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Includes patients across a wide uACR and eGFR range, with and without T2D or CVD, and with or without RAAS inhibitor use. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 21–23. | Footnotes: 1-3 | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.21-23
#: 193 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE slowed eGFR decline over time in patients with CKD with or without type 2 diabetes. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Long-term eGFR slope outcome from EMPA-KIDNEY. Annual decline presented in the asset: -1.37 with JARDIANCE versus -2.75 mL/min/1.73 m²/year with placebo. Use the complete outcome qualification. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 27–29. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.27-29
#: 194 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE can help protect kidney function in patients with CKD who have low albuminuria. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Linked to slowed eGFR decline across the uACR spectrum. The primary composite subgroup result was not statistically significant in the uACR &lt;30 mg/g subgroup; retain the eGFR-slope qualification. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 33–36. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY | PC-CRP-105591, pp.33-36
#: 195 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE reduced kidney disease progression regardless of diabetes status. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Based on a subsidiary EMPA-KIDNEY analysis across causes of CKD. The analysis type and outcome definition must remain linked. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 37–39. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPA-KIDNEY subsidiary analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.37-39
#: 196 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE may slow the onset of dialysis by more than 20 years in selected patients with CKD. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Modelled extrapolation based on EMPA-KIDNEY eGFR slope, not an observed clinical-trial endpoint. Must always be described as extrapolated and not as a guaranteed individual outcome. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 40–46. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: Extrapolated EMPA-KIDNEY eGFR-slope analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.40-46
#: 197 | Final Corrected Claim: In the EMPOWER meta-analysis, JARDIANCE reduced the risk of acute kidney injury by 27% and the risk of a 50% or greater increase in serum creatinine by 20%. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Heart failure; Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Meta-analysis across CKD, HF and T2D + eCVD populations. AKI HR=0.73; 95% CI: 0.63, 0.85. Creatinine increase HR=0.80; 95% CI: 0.72, 0.88. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 60–62. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPOWER meta-analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.60-62
#: 198 | Final Corrected Claim: In the EMPOWER meta-analysis, JARDIANCE reduced the risk of kidney failure by 34% and kidney disease progression by 30%. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Heart failure; Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Meta-analysis across CKD, HF and T2D + eCVD populations. Kidney failure HR=0.66; 95% CI: 0.55, 0.79. Kidney disease progression HR=0.70; 95% CI: 0.63, 0.78. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 63–65. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: EMPOWER meta-analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.63-65
#: 199 | Final Corrected Claim: The risk of selected serious adverse events with JARDIANCE remained low and comparable with placebo in more than 20,000 patients. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease; Heart failure; Type 2 diabetes; Cardiovascular risk / established CVD | Key Message Type: Safety / Tolerability | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Meta-analysis statement covering selected serious adverse events. It does not replace the complete locally approved safety information. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 66–68. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: Safety outcomes meta-analysis | PC-CRP-105591, pp.66-68
#: 200 | Final Corrected Claim: The 2024 KDIGO guideline reinforces SGLT2 inhibitors as an early and foundational therapy for the management of CKD. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Guideline / Standard of care | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Class-level recommendation applying to defined patient groups by eGFR, albuminuria, T2D and HF status. Avoid implying an exclusive recommendation for JARDIANCE. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 72–75. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: KDIGO 2024 Clinical Practice Guideline for CKD | PC-CRP-105591, pp.72-75
#: 201 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE is a once-daily oral treatment with no titration, can be taken at any time of day with or without food, and can be initiated down to an eGFR of 20 mL/min/1.73 m². | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Dosing / Administration | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: The asset presents 10 mg once daily as the starting and recommended dose. Initiation and continuation thresholds must be checked against the current local label. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 76–78. | Footnotes: 1,2 | Reference: JARDIANCE Summary of Product Characteristics, June 2025 | PC-CRP-105591, pp.76-78
#: 202 | Final Corrected Claim: JARDIANCE works by inhibiting SGLT2" which is the title of the slide and next point is "JARDIANCE reduces glucose and sodium reabsorption and increases delivery of sodium to the distal tubule | Status: Corrected | Indication: Type 2 diabetes; Chronic kidney disease; Heart failure | Key Message Type: Mechanism of action | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Linked in the asset to increased urinary glucose excretion, tubuloglomerular feedback and reduced intraglomerular pressure. Proposed cardiovascular mechanisms should not be presented as proven clinical mediators. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 79–81. | Footnotes: 1 | Reference: JARDIANCE Summary of Product Characteristics | PC-CRP-105591, pp.79-81
#: 203 | Final Corrected Claim: In EMPA-KIDNEY, JARDIANCE reduced first and recurrent all-cause hospitalisation by 14% versus placebo. | Status: Confirmed complete | Indication: Chronic kidney disease | Key Message Type: Efficacy / Clinical benefit | End Audience: HCP / Internal | Contextual Information: Key secondary outcome including first and all subsequent all-cause hospitalisations. HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.78, 0.95; p=0.003. Source: PC-CRP-105591, pages 121–123. | Footnotes: 1,2 | Reference: Herrington WG et al. N Engl J Med. 2023; 388:117-127 | Data on file | PC-CRP-105591, pp.121-123</data>
