<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:section:e5e1003e-f1ba-47e7-9743-0582ab6b81b9">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Generic name</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">28</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">e5e1003e-f1ba-47e7-9743-0582ab6b81b9</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b</data>
  <data key="d16">If the generic name (empagliflozin) is required by regulatory authorities to appear with the brand name, then the generic name must always appear with the largest display of the JARDIANCE logo on any surface or screen and should be at least one-third the size of the logotype.

Always use brown for the generic name unless local regulations or technical requirements state otherwise. Please follow individual country guidelines regarding use of the generic name.</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:section:f2c02b8c-bf99-49af-a05d-badfccf6119a">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Registration mark</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">28</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">f2c02b8c-bf99-49af-a05d-badfccf6119a</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b</data>
  <data key="d16">The JARDIANCE logo has a registration mark that appears at the end of the brand name, showing that the brand is a registered trademark. In some countries, the registration mark is required whenever the JARDIANCE brand name appears, while in other countries it may be required only on first appearance within a document or first appearance on each new page, spread, or screen.

For internal pieces, the registration mark and generic name are not required after the first mention. For your country-specific regulations, please contact the Corporate Department, Trademarks &amp;amp; Unfair Competition for guidance prior to use.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

This symbol forms an important part of the logo, must appear in the size and position shown, and must be scaled up or down in proportion to the size of the logo.</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
</node>
