<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:section:657db29d-9654-4480-b84d-6c3fcd470025">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Branding elements:</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">38</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">657db29d-9654-4480-b84d-6c3fcd470025</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b</data>
  <data key="d16"></data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:section:acfb835d-97bf-45d9-8e82-330c79132d9e">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Colours: technical instructions</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">38</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">acfb835d-97bf-45d9-8e82-330c79132d9e</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b</data>
  <data key="d16">It is important to use the brand palette whenever possible. Best practice is to apply colours at 100% strength for maximum brand recognition; however, tints and shades may be used to enhance visual impact where necessary in both print and digital applications.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:section:3b09ab45-eeba-4d46-bdee-4a574aabfbae">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">The JARDIANCE way</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">38</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">3b09ab45-eeba-4d46-bdee-4a574aabfbae</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b</data>
  <data key="d16">-   Use full 100% brand colours wherever possible for maximum consistency and recognition
-   Apply tints and shades only when they enhance clarity, hierarchy, or visual balance
-   Verify colour contrast meets accessibility standards in all digital applications

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:section:b968e3b9-cd56-4b60-9314-7ee065e01a5f">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">The WRONG way</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">38</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">b968e3b9-cd56-4b60-9314-7ee065e01a5f</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b</data>
  <data key="d16">- DON'T change R/G/B or C/M/Y/K tones manually; when changing shades, please make sure to use transparency settings (for R/G/B) or tint settings (for C/M/Y/K)
- DON'T use tints or shades in a way that reduces legibility or weakens the brand's visual impact

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
</node>
