<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:section:66ad13f4-f620-4999-8bdd-31026196938b">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Introduction to family branding</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">67</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">66ad13f4-f620-4999-8bdd-31026196938b</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">b5acf5ff-42d8-4d92-bba4-931955176f5b</data>
  <data key="d16">The global branding system applies to the 'JARDIANCE family' in a way that visually depicts the relationship between the Boehringer Ingelheim/Lilly Alliance and among its related product brands in the Diabetes Portfolio.

There are 3 products that comprise the JARDIANCE family, with JARDIANCE being the lead brand and SYNJARDY and GLYXAMBI as line extensions:

- JARDIANCE ®  (empagliflozin)
- SYNJARDY ®  (empagliflozin/metformin HCl)
- GLYXAMBI ®  (empagliflozin/linagliptin)

This section highlights the specific JARDIANCE family branding elements, explains the rationale behind them, and provides detailed instructions for approved use to ensure consistency throughout all communications.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

Keep in mind that when any of the family brands are used in combination with JARDIANCE, the JARDIANCE branding elements (eg, colour, environment, page architecture) must be adhered to.

Important: please note that the Boehringer Ingelheim/Lilly Alliance is not currently pursuing future heart failure or chronic kidney disease indications for SYNJARDY or GLYXAMBI. There are no updates to design or branding on family brands.</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">JARDIANCE Brand Book 2025.pdf</data>
</node>
