<node id="urn:kg:jardiance:section:6a79446a-a696-4ec4-a11f-5dee0e4e5120">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Empagliflozin in patients inadequately controlled with metformin and linagliptin</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">17</data>
  <data key="d9">product_information</data>
  <data key="d10">6a79446a-a696-4ec4-a11f-5dee0e4e5120</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">98de1eab-c096-475d-9a30-ff5319cefc40</data>
  <data key="d16">In patients inadequately controlled with metformin and linagliptin 5 mg, treatment with both empagliflozin 10 mg or 25 mg resulted in statistically significant (p &amp;lt; 0.0001) reductions in HbA1c and body weight compared to placebo (Table 5). In addition it resulted in clinically meaningful reductions in FPG, systolic and diastolic blood pressure compared to placebo.

Table 5: Efficacy results of a 24 week placebo-controlled study in patients inadequately controlled</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">jardiance</data>
  <data key="d5">jardiance-epar-product-information_en.pdf</data>
</node>
