M, Adamo M, et al. Eur Heart J. 2023.", "Content Modules &amp; Rule Sets": "NA"}}, {"row_number": 83, "cells": {"Resource": "Moumita", "Name": "CL-CRP-001483", "Match Text": "Optimised treatment should go beyond HbA1c reduction and help protect your patients with T2D and CVD", "Country of Origin": "Corporate", "Brand": "JARDIANCE", "Therapeutic Area": "Metabolism", "Lifecycle State": "Approved for Use", "Indication": null, "Key Message Type": "CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic, Efficacy, Guidelines", "End Audience": null, "Contextual Information": null, "Footnotes": "CVD=cardiovascular; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; T2D=type 2 diabetes", "Reference": "2022 - Management of Hyperglycemia in Type 2 Diabetes, 2022. A Consensus Report by the American Diab", "AMA Style Guide References": "Management of Hyperglycemia in Type 2 Diabetes, 2022. A Consensus Report by the American Diab. 2022.", "Content Modules &amp; Rule Sets": "NA"}}, {"row_number": 84, "cells": {"Resource": "Moumita", "Name": "CL-CRP-001485", "Match Text": "JARDIANCE is a guideline-recommended treatment for patients with HF across the LVEF spectrum, with or without T2D", "Country of Origin": "Corporate", "Brand": "JARDIANCE", "Therapeutic Area": "Metabolism", "Lifecycle State": "Approved for Use", "Indication": null, "Key Message Type": "Guidelines", "End Audience": "HCP (Health Care Personnel)", "Contextual Information": null, "Footnotes": "HF=heart failure; LVEF=left ventricular ejection fraction; T2D=type 2 diabetes", "Reference": "2022 - McDonagh TA httpsacademic.oup.comeurheartjarticle423635996358045\n\nMcDonagh TA, Metra M, Adamo M, et al. Eur Heart J 2023", "AMA Style Guide References": "McDonagh TA httpsacademic.oup.comeurheartjarticle423635996358045. 2022.\n\nMcDonagh TA, Metra M, Adamo M, et al. Eur Heart J. 2023.", "Content Modules &amp; Rule Sets": "NA"}}, {"row_number": 85, "cells": {"Resource": "Moumita", "Name": "CL-CRP-001489", "Match Text": "The risk of CV death in patients increases with progression of T2D or CKD", "Country of Origin": "Corporate", "Brand": "JARDIANCE", "Therapeutic Area": "Metabolism", "Lifecycle State": "Approved for Use", "Indication": null, "Key Message Type": "CRM/Cardio-Renal-Metabolic", "End Audience": "HCP (Health Care Personnel)", "Contextual Information": null, "Footnotes": "CKD=chronic kidney disease; CV=cardiovascular; T2D=type 2 diabetes", "Reference": "Raghavan J Am Heart Assoc 2019\n\nMatsushita Nat Rev Nephrol 2022", "AMA Style Guide References": "Raghavan J Am Heart Assoc. 2019.\n\nMatsushita Nat Rev Nephrol. 2022.", "Content Modules &amp; Rule Sets": "NA"}}, {"row_number": 86, "cells": {"Resource": "Moumita", "Name": "CL-CRP-001492", "Match Text": "Primary care guidelines recommend including SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, as part of initial therapy for patients with T2D at high or very high cardiovascular risk", "Country of Origin": "Corporate", "Brand": "JARDIANCE", "Therapeutic Area": "Metabolism", "Lifecycle State": "Approved for Use", "Indication": null, "Key Message Type": "Guidelines", "End Audience": "HCP (Health Care Personnel)", "Contextual Information": null, "Footnotes": "SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 inhibitor; T2D=type 2 diabetes", "Reference": "Seidu S i wsp. Prim Care Diabetes 2022;16:223", "AMA Style Guide References": "Seidu S i wsp. Prim Care Diabetes. 2022;16:223.", "Content Modules &amp; Rule Sets": "NA"}}, {"row_number": 87, "cells": {"Resource": "Moumita", "Name": "CL-CRP-001484", "Match Text": "In patients with T2D and eCVD, JARDIANCE reduced risk of CV death regardless of patients’ HbA1c or BMI.", "Country of Origin": "Corporate", "Brand": "JARDIANCE", "Therapeutic Area": "Metabolism", "Lifecycle State": "Approved for Use", "Indication": "Type 2 diabetes mellitus", "Key Message Type": "Efficacy", "End Audience": "HCP (Health Care Personnel)", "Contextual Information": null, "Footnotes": "In the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial, a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled study of 7720 patients with T2D at high cardiovascular risk, the efficacy and safety of JARDIANCE 10 mg or 25 mg (n=4867) were evaluated vs placebo (n=2333). Patients were adults with insufficiently controlled T2D and CAD, PAD, or a history of MI or stroke. The primary composite outcome in the EMPA-REG OUTCOME trial was 3-point MACE, composed of death from CV causes, nonfatal MI, or nonfatal stroke, as analysed in the pooled JARDIANCE group vs the placebo group. The 14% RRR (1.6% ARR) in 3-point MACE (HR=0.86; 95% CI: 0.74, 0.99; p&lt;0.001 for noninferiority; p=0.04 for superiority) was driven by a reduction in the risk of CV death (HR=0.62; 95% CI: 0.49, 0.77); there was no change in risk of nonfatal MI (HR=0.87; 95% CI: 0.70, 1.09) or nonfatal stroke (HR=1.24; 95% CI: 0.92, 1.67).  A prespecified analysis included subgroups of patients with HbA1c &lt;8.5% and ≥8.5%  Rate of CV death (%) across HbA1c subgroups: All values depict JARDIANCE vs placebo, respectively. &lt;7.0%: 2.4 (n=297) vs 7.9 (n=127); 7.0%-&lt;8.0%: 3.7 (n=2042) vs 6.1 (n=1029); 8.0%-&lt;9.0%: 3.7 (n=1534) vs 5.4 (n=795); ≥9.0%: 4.2 (n=812) vs 5.5 (n=382).  Rate of CV death across BMI subgroups: In the BMI ≥30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate of CV death was 3.8% for JARDIANCE (n=2408) vs 4.8% for placebo (n=1213). In the BMI &lt;30 kg/m2 subgroup, the rate of CV death was 3.5% for JARDIANCE (n=2279) vs 6.9% for placebo (n=1120).   RRR=relative risk reduction; ARR=absolute risk reduction; BMI=body mass index; CAD=coronary artery disease; CI=confidence interval; CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; HR=hazard ratio; MACE=major adverse cardiovascular events; MI=myocardial infarction; PAD=peripheral artery disease; T2D=type 2 diabetes", "Reference": "2015 - Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes\n\nZinman N Engl J Med 2015 Supplement\n\nInzucchi Circulation 2018\n\n", "AMA Style Guide References": "Empagliflozin, Cardiovascular Outcomes, and Mortality in Type 2 Diabetes. 2015.\n\nZinman N Engl J Med. 2015 Supplement.\n\nInzucchi Circulation. 2018.", "Content Modules &amp; Rule Sets": "NA"}}, {"row_number": 88, "cells": {"Resource": "Moumita", "Name": "CL-CRP-001486", "Match Text": "SGLT2is, such as JARDIANCE, are Class I recommended for first-line use in patients with eCVD + T2D to reduce the risk of CV events", "Country of Origin": "Corporate", "Brand": "JARDIANCE", "Therapeutic Area": "Metabolism", "Lifecycle State": "Approved for Use", "Indication": null, "Key Message Type": "Guidelines", "End Audience": "HCP (Health Care Personnel)", "Contextual Information": null, "Footnotes": "CV=cardiovascular; eCVD=established cardiovascular disease; ESC=European Society of Cardiology; HbA1c=haemoglobin A1c; SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor; T2D=type 2 diabetes", "Reference": "Marx Eur Heart J 2023", "AMA Style Guide References": "Marx Eur Heart J. 2023.", "Content Modules &amp; Rule Sets": "NA"}}, {"row_number": 89, "cells": {"Resource": "Moumita", "Name": "CL-CRP-001487", "Match Text": "SGLT2is are a Class I, Level A-recommended therapy for patients with HFrEF to reduce the risk of heart failure hospitalisation or cardiovascular death, making JARDIANCE 1 of 4 foundational treatments for HFrEF", "Country of Origin": "Corporate", "Brand": "JARDIANCE", "Therapeutic Area": "Metabolism", "Lifecycle State": "Approved for Use", "Indication": null, "Key Message Type": "Guidelines", "End Audience": "HCP (Health Care Personnel)", "Contextual Information": null, "Footnotes": "HFrEF=heart failure with reduced ejection fraction;SGLT2i=sodium-glucose cotransporter-2 inhibitor", "Reference": "2022 - McDonagh TA httpsacademic.oup.comeurheartjarticle423635996358045", "AMA Style Guide References": "McDonagh TA httpsacademic.oup.comeurheartjarticle423635996358045. 2022.", "Content Modules &amp; Rule Sets": "NA"}}, {"row_number": 90, "cells": {"Resource": "Moumita", "Name": "CL-CRP-001499", "Match Text": "The risk of CV death triples in pa