<node id="urn:kg:ofev:chunk:bd820940-f6f3-41cb-b2d6-94d1c93fb8f2">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">158</data>
  <data key="d7">252</data>
  <data key="d8">64</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">aba56e41-f812-4087-864d-9b80c5b0eaf8</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">b5feb6982969ccf19d244cc2dc883bbb917882f337e777549af3554117ffcf8a</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d15">bd820940-f6f3-41cb-b2d6-94d1c93fb8f2</data>
  <data key="d16">The campaign visual works to clearly communicate the unstable and unpredictable nature of IPF. The visual features a man walking on ice that is beginning to crack behind him. The ice symbolizes the uncertain and harsh landscape of IPF, while the cracks in the ice represent the unpredictable and severe outcomes for patients with IPF.

The campaign is flexible and can be utilized across all unbranded communications. The artwork is able to accommodate large areas and can also be cropped around the man walking on ice when needed. However, it is advised that the cracks of ice not be cropped too much so that the impact of the visual is not lost.

The campaign headline should always accompany the visual (see 6.6 for headline).

Additional artwork is available for the sheet of ice without the patient or ice cracks. This can be used when the full campaign is not needed.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

ExAMPLES oF cAMPAiGn ViSuAL in ProMotionAL MAtEriALS

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

icE SHEEt ArtWorK

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
