<node id="urn:kg:ofev:chunk:e8cc6b6b-9ccd-40ce-8f78-568952d99462">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">168</data>
  <data key="d7">85</data>
  <data key="d8">69</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">ac548616-122c-4ca0-a4c3-01eb83b4a49a</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">d1d30e206b85753af72f6bd4bbc67553cd9c3a688e0878482f4890d2de63c060</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d15">e8cc6b6b-9ccd-40ce-8f78-568952d99462</data>
  <data key="d16">The patient unbranded identity system comprises key assets that are designed, managed, and used in all of our disease education communication materials.

Our identity system unifies our unbranded materials in a consistent, flexible, and ownable way across all channels, allowing us to communicate consistently to the IPF patient community.</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:chunk:92a5d3fd-9710-4116-bade-2f5854c2a3c4">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">169</data>
  <data key="d7">137</data>
  <data key="d8">70</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">8ef37cfd-36e8-4299-b27a-c20c73cbb5b9</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">cffb22fe9f21e8c290546f83f35de90cf33a520a5caf939efa8c9cbde0788ada</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d15">92a5d3fd-9710-4116-bade-2f5854c2a3c4</data>
  <data key="d16">Typography is another important element of our unbranded patient identity and a way to communicate our personality.

The Museo type family was selected for its friendliness and unique letterforms. They are also extremely legible in various font sizes.

In applications such as Microsoft ®  Word, Microsoft ®  PowerPoint, and programs with restrictive font sets, use Arial Regular for body text and Arial Bold for headline, subtitle, and subheadline text. Museo can be purchased as a Typekit ®  Web font for Web use from typekit.com.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
