<node id="urn:kg:ofev:chunk:ce48a9ed-8c5d-4c57-b053-e0d1e6035b56">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">193</data>
  <data key="d7">64</data>
  <data key="d8">86</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">3379ee4f-b2e1-4db9-8e67-7a79ea26d2c5</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">8c2210faba01868f26204f81a1988da4b80f385edf233d11ebed89d217af9a60</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d15">ce48a9ed-8c5d-4c57-b053-e0d1e6035b56</data>
  <data key="d16">Clinical trial visual identity assets include more than just color and typography. The secondary graphics for the clinical trials provide an ownable and recognizable look-beyond the logo-that can be used on all study-related communications.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:chunk:d8534697-6adc-4605-b9e0-01dbcd22097e">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">194</data>
  <data key="d7">96</data>
  <data key="d8">87</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">76eba09f-7bc3-4db1-a3c1-f29d47d0686b</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">10619a0b2305c7edd9232fec2563505aa2a9cfe233d2d94541a52d4c89f364a7</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d15">d8534697-6adc-4605-b9e0-01dbcd22097e</data>
  <data key="d16">Our secondary graphics have been designed to accommodate a variety of layouts and content. The size of the shapes can be scaled up, down, and sideways, adding flexibility to the system while maintaining a consistent look.

Blue should always be the dominant color on the page; the golden supergraphic should be used as a secondary element.

oFEV\_HorizontAL\_cMYK.Ai

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:chunk:acdcfc77-a332-4305-8663-905db766ac16">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d6">195</data>
  <data key="d7">78</data>
  <data key="d8">88</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">1e45624e-d809-4909-a45f-11c6fffa514e</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">87c386c69b6f4eaf13fc568a3a43dacf1625d79bc5e840dcc2c724feb299ef06</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d15">acdcfc77-a332-4305-8663-905db766ac16</data>
  <data key="d16">The key elements of the clinical trial materials are the secondary graphics (the dominant blue color and the golden supergraphic), the clinical trial logo, and the written content. These elements complement one another and work synergistically to communicate in a clear and compelling way.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

.

Y</data>
  <data key="d3">Chunk</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
