<node id="urn:kg:ofev:pisection:6ad4dd31-dcd4-4ea0-bc69-54a13057e025">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Time to First Acute ILD Exacerbation</data>
  <data key="d8">25</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">6ad4dd31-dcd4-4ea0-bc69-54a13057e025</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c</data>
  <data key="d16">Acute ILD exacerbation was defined as unexplained worsening or development of dyspnea within 30 days, new diffuse pulmonary infiltrates on chest x-ray, and/or new HRCT parenchymal abnormalities with no pneumothorax or pleural effusion, and exclusion of alternative causes. Acute ILD exacerbations were not adjudicated.

The risk of first acute ILD exacerbation did not show a statistically significant difference between the OFEV group compared to placebo (52 week treatment period: HR 0.72, (95% CI: 0.38, 1.37); whole trial: HR 0.63 (95% CI: 0.37, 1.07)).</data>
  <data key="d3">PISection</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:pisection:d98137e4-1182-40a9-a960-56289cab694d">
