<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:33bb5a4c-1bc7-4deb-9837-fc2b82a09da8">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d19">body</data>
  <data key="d8">39</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">33bb5a4c-1bc7-4deb-9837-fc2b82a09da8</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">4.2</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:32bd715c-cf39-431e-9310-aaf5b8a5ece9">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Campaign Visual</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">39</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">32bd715c-cf39-431e-9310-aaf5b8a5ece9</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">The campaign visual works to clearly communicate the slowing of disease progression with OFEV ® . The campaign shows a declining path, which represents the continuous and irreversible deterioration of lung function in patients with IPF. The path is changed by the intervention of the hand, which lifts and supports the patient as he enjoys time with his grandson, an activity that is common, but not always possible for many patients with IPF. The hand that is changing the path can be interpreted as the HCP, OFEV ® , or Boehringer Ingelheim.

Together, the downward angle of the path, in contrast with the angle of the inset image of the patient, represents the reduction in lung function decline and the slowing of disease progression with OFEV ® .

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:4d71ac10-b21b-4158-8cc7-cb4ab975a68a">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d19">body</data>
  <data key="d8">40</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">4d71ac10-b21b-4158-8cc7-cb4ab975a68a</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">4.3</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:867e2dbb-dff0-4a67-a359-bd8580ba9d15">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Image Library</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">40</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">867e2dbb-dff0-4a67-a359-bd8580ba9d15</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">Several additional visuals are available to provide variety within a consistent campaign style. Each image has been carefully chosen to show patients with IPF engaging in activities that are both credible and compelling for this population.</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:aedd0ddd-2309-405b-9b27-36237e738956">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Direction for conducting localised green screen photoshoot</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">40</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">aedd0ddd-2309-405b-9b27-36237e738956</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">In the event that there is a need to use a different patient type or activity level within the context of this background imagery, new photography can be retouched into the existing backgrounds. Here are some general guidelines for photography if this need arises.

1.  Studio: Talent may be photographed against a plain, white, seamless background
2. Camera: Use a medium format camera with an 80 mm lens
3. Camera position: Set camera 12 to 13 feet from subject, approximately at height of subject's waist
4. Lighting: To match lighting conditions of the backgrounds, use a hard light high up on camera left to emulate sunlight and a fill light lower on camera right

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

