<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:d0e2e3e6-2ebe-4713-b6f8-d24ba5da6d07">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Market-Specific Adaptations</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">56</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">d0e2e3e6-2ebe-4713-b6f8-d24ba5da6d07</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">In some markets, local regulatory requirements may influence the design of promotional materials. Some countries may have restrictions on the use of patient photography or the use of brand colors. This page provides examples of how the patient brand assets may be adapted within our system.

Regardless of the use of patient photography or brand colors, designs are unified by the use of key branding elements.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

PAtiEnt MAtEriAL WitH PHotoGrAPHY

this is the preferred design. it should be used in countries that have no restrictions on the use of promotional branding assets. the design is consistent with the HcP branding and may incorporate the logo, branding colors, holding shape, line pattern, illustrations, and patient photography.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

PAtiEnt MAtEriAL WitH PHotoGrAPHY And ALtErnAtE coLor PALEttE

this branding option should be used in countries that cannot use brand colors but can use patient photography. the design includes the holding shape, line pattern, and patient photography.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

PAtiEnt MAtEriAL WitHout PHotoGrAPHY

this is the preferred design for markets that are

not permitted to use photography. the design is consistent with the HcP branding and may incorporate the logo, branding colors, holding shape, line pattern, and illustrations.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

PAtiEnt MAtEriAL WitHout PHotoGrAPHY And WitH ALtErnAtE coLor PALEttE

this option should be used in countries that have restrictions on the use of both patient photography and branding colors. it may incorporate the holding shape and line pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:681f4c2c-8132-4a89-b73f-4ee7735ddb85">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">General information about the safe and effective use of OFEV.</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">32</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">681f4c2c-8132-4a89-b73f-4ee7735ddb85</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c</data>
  <data key="d16">Medicines are sometimes prescribed for purposes other than those listed in a Patient Information leaflet. Do not use OFEV for a condition for which it was not prescribed. Do not give OFEV to other people, even if they have the same symptoms you have. It may harm them. This Patient Information leaflet summarizes the most important information about OFEV. If you would like more information, talk to your doctor. You can ask your pharmacist or doctor for information about OFEV that is written for health professionals.

For more information about OFEV, including the current prescribing information, and patient support, go to www.ofev.com/support or call Boehringer Ingelheim Pharmaceuticals, Inc. at 1-800-542-6257, or scan the code to go to www.ofev.com/support .

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
