<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:5d73ab60-4648-4da2-9902-581f07f9629f">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Color Palette</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">19</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">5d73ab60-4648-4da2-9902-581f07f9629f</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">The OFEV ®  colors were selected to reinforce our brand identity and to differentiate our brand from competitors. They should be used to help maintain brand recognition and impact. The OFEV ®  core brand color is Guardian Blue, and it should be the most prominent color in the palette. In addition, Guardian Blue is the only color that should be used with the line pattern.

The three secondary colors, Inspiring Yellow, Brilliant Gold, and Premium Orange, reflect the colors used in the OFEV ®  gradient. Premium Orange may be used for highlights in applications as well as in typographical call-outs and subheads.

Comfort Gray is included as a neutral tertiary color that helps balance the palette. Comfort Gray can be used in clinical and scientific situations, such as in charts or to represent placebo.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:b56615fb-ea88-4be1-b049-104d7fe47534">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">2.10</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">20</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">b56615fb-ea88-4be1-b049-104d7fe47534</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16"></data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:b6c67302-a0f0-4c66-aa02-059141f00da2">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Secondary Graphics</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">20</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">b6c67302-a0f0-4c66-aa02-059141f00da2</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">A secondary graphic is a brand element that symbolizes our personality and unifies our brand across all communications. Our secondary graphic is a combination of two geometric shapes: the Guardian Blue shape that appears on the bottom of the page, and the golden gradient shape that appears on the top of the page. Together, these two shapes create a space that represents the change OFEV ®  is creating in the path of IPF.

The two shapes that make up our secondary graphic should appear together on every communication piece. The Guardian Blue shape should never appear on a page without the golden gradient shape and vice versa.

Our secondary graphic has been provided in both a vertical and a horizontal format for flexibility of use (see next page).

&lt;!-- image --&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:70a9ffe8-bf36-4b7d-bb8b-cbccd27959a0">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">2.11</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">21</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">70a9ffe8-bf36-4b7d-bb8b-cbccd27959a0</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16"></data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:e3f4c465-5528-4fc3-b8f6-39435ba74bce">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Secondary Graphics Flexibility</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">21</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">e3f4c465-5528-4fc3-b8f6-39435ba74bce</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">Our secondary graphic has been designed to accommodate a variety of layouts and content. The shapes can be scaled up and down, adding flexibility to the system and allowing for different configurations of the shapes to provide a variety of layout options with a consistent look.

The Guardian Blue shape should always be dominant and the golden gradient shape should be used as an accent. The golden gradient shape should not take up more than 15% of the page.

&lt;!-- image --&gt;

oFEV\_HorizontAL\_cMYK.Ai</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:15a37819-56b0-4631-9f09-a8b180c3adb9">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">2.12</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">22</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">15a37819-56b0-4631-9f09-a8b180c3adb9</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
