<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:5c96615a-f77b-4894-b50e-67747b31d772">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Change from Baseline in Percent Predicted Forced Vital Capacity</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">19</data>
  <data key="d9">prescribing_information</data>
  <data key="d10">5c96615a-f77b-4894-b50e-67747b31d772</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_PI.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">c0db5dd8-583e-47bb-9b75-58402a32791c</data>
  <data key="d16">Figure 2 presents the cumulative distribution for all cut-offs for the change from baseline in FVC percent predicted at Week 52 for Study 2. For all categorical declines in lung function, the proportion of patients declining was lower on OFEV than on placebo. Study 3 showed similar results.</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_PI.pdf</data>
</node>
<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:1b4a09eb-d493-4fc2-bfc7-8b41f7459cc9">
