<node id="urn:kg:ofev:section:beaac254-f209-4cd1-887a-843966bcfb18">
  <data key="d0">brand</data>
  <data key="d20">Color Palette</data>
  <data key="d19">heading</data>
  <data key="d8">85</data>
  <data key="d9">brand_book</data>
  <data key="d10">beaac254-f209-4cd1-887a-843966bcfb18</data>
  <data key="d11">docling</data>
  <data key="d12">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
  <data key="d14">7c99d579-1450-4667-9bc5-7d13421ddab2</data>
  <data key="d16">The clinical trial colors are the same as our brand colors. They should be used to help maintain brand recognition and impact, and to establish a visual link between the brand and the clinical trials.

In this color palette, Inspiring Yellow and Brilliant Gold are the primary colors and should be the most prominent colors in the color palette.

Guardian Blue is a secondary color and Premium Orange may be used for highlights in applications as well as in typographical call-outs and subheads.

Comfort Gray is included again as a neutral tertiary color that helps balance the palette. Comfort Gray can be used in clinical and scientific situations such as charts or to represent placebo.

INPULSIS COLOR PALETTE</data>
  <data key="d3">Section</data>
  <data key="d4">ofev</data>
  <data key="d5">OFEV_Brand-Book_Nov-2015.pdf</data>
</node>
